# 2000 tasks parked on their own channels are released in a shuffled order,
# with 400 more spawned between the releases: fibers past the pool of idle
# stacks tear down in an order unrelated to their registration, and each one
# leaves the live thread registry in O(1) (Thread.jet thread_unregister_tcb).
# Every task returns what it was sent and no thread is left behind: after
# tasks.quiesce() the thread count equals the one read before any task. The
# quiesce returns once every scheduler thread, retired carriers included, has
# left the process (Scheduler.jet jet_rt_scheduler_shutdown), so no wall-time
# wait and no pool pin is needed. Same output on jet run and at O0, O1 and O2.
fixture: Fixtures/Teardown
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
env: JETPACK_ROOT={work}/jetpack
step: jet run main.jet
exit: 0
stdout: = "2000 of 2000 and 400 of 400 returned what they were sent\nthreads unchanged true\n"
step: jet build -O0 main.jet
exit: 0
step o0: built
exit: 0
stdout: = "2000 of 2000 and 400 of 400 returned what they were sent\nthreads unchanged true\n"
step: jet build -O1 main.jet
exit: 0
step o1: built
exit: 0
stdout: = "2000 of 2000 and 400 of 400 returned what they were sent\nthreads unchanged true\n"
step: jet build --release main.jet
exit: 0
step o2: built
exit: 0
stdout: = "2000 of 2000 and 400 of 400 returned what they were sent\nthreads unchanged true\n"
